The #999 fix was already done in commit cfedd194 before the interruption, so I didn't redo or recommit anything. I only checked it.

What the commit changed: the top-level agent's limits now come from main_agent_execution_limits() in src/agent_builder.rs.
• **Token cap:** removed (`usize::MAX`, was `1_000_000`). It counted context re-sent every turn, so it stopped runs around turn 16 at a 60K context (seen as `1061497/1000000`).
• **10-minute limit:** removed. It's now set explicitly to `Duration::MAX` instead of quietly inheriting yoagent 0.24.2's 600s default. I checked that yoagent only compares against this value (elapsed >= self.limits.max_duration, context.rs:1213) and never adds it to a time, so the huge value can't overflow and panic. yoyo itself does no arithmetic on it either.
• **Turn cap:** unchanged (--max-turns, else 200), and loop detection stays on.
• **Other agents:** the two `with_max_turns(1)` agents weren't touched. Sub-agents still have yoagent's built-in caps (1M tokens / 300s); the code comment says changing them needs yoagent#238 (in 0.24.3, which yoyo doesn't use yet).

Checks I re-ran:
• `cargo build, cargo test (no failures), cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings and cargo fmt -- --check` all pass.
• The three tests in src/agent_limits_tests.rs pass: default limits, a Some(37) near-miss, and a check that the token cap is above 1,061,497.
• I didn't re-run the test where the old 1_000_000 is put back. The commit message says it turned those tests red by name.

Docs: searching docs/src and README.md for 1_000_000, 1,000,000, max_total_tokens or 10 min finds one line: the new history note in docs/src/configuration/skills.md, which is correct. The commit also fixed a wrong default on that page (--max-turns said 50; it's 200) and added a CHANGELOG line.

Issue: #999 is closed, and the closing comment names cfedd194 and says the sub-agent caps are still open.

